{"objects":[{"id":"flow","instance":"instance--b96dad5f-c519-5a1f-a718-912ca4a86c02","objects":["attack-action--1","attack-action--2","attack-action--3","attack-action--4","attack-action--5","attack-action--6","attack-condition--1","instance--61de4ecc-fa23-5e7e-ae06-4dea6f8fa7bb","software--ad-domain-controller","instance--0f98e79d-d02b-5946-bd01-ed49de5d5f6c","instance--7b06b1c8-ca68-5c3b-a1eb-c1e885835158","software--mimikatz","instance--9bbdb272-4ec4-5d34-b458-ef38ff9db2e0","software--kdc","instance--58119790-6137-5708-9889-fa140694de27","instance--3536a568-610f-5570-bba9-6dfe97bc9c2e","instance--384798bd-a84b-5feb-8d38-7f9d0a087f11","instance--ed6039fe-678b-5ae9-9576-73e6ea35b0c8","instance--7e8c9301-c3f8-55e9-8894-e81f1b6203d9","instance--b6d82c28-0a68-5c6f-b058-c1e072f51852","instance--fb1118d0-336c-5935-b063-da32890e1042","instance--3ed72a13-e3e4-5655-9e15-4debdde7cb93","instance--32877dd9-1956-59de-992f-5f6605ce2624","instance--73f01366-fe5c-5356-8c8f-bceb54f6fdcd","instance--2d2c3f9a-0c42-5937-89bc-bb8238381f2e","instance--48ede1c4-c823-5557-b6f1-088d5cdfc7c0","instance--7192f500-a2e4-5d89-b61d-2813e196a38d","instance--f9c4e00c-2c11-5ba6-a32c-55dc52b437eb","instance--ba8567f8-ba07-5d4a-9147-29dcb92249c2"],"properties":[["name","KRBTGT hash abuse to forge Golden Tickets"],["description","The article explains how attackers target the KRBTGT account after compromising a Domain Controller, obtain the KRBTGT password hash, and use it to generate forged Kerberos TGTs (Golden Tickets) with arbitrary group membership and long lifetimes for persistence and access across the domain."],["scope","incident"],["author",[["name","Sean Metcalf"]]],["external_references",[["item-1",[["source_name","adsecurity.org"],["url","https://adsecurity.org/?p=483"]]]]]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--ad592d05-6969-5b51-98a8-1ad9b6aab896","120":"instance--5850a8f4-8241-5e73-9bf0-dcd376cd5025","150":"instance--0da1498f-3beb-5916-a249-e0410a4a81e4","180":"instance--d3632784-7391-5a29-83e2-edab51db56c6","210":"instance--8bc47ca5-ca73-5a04-a9ea-918608f10871","240":"instance--6546eef6-c5ad-516e-a417-89916e651648","270":"instance--244e5a69-f465-564e-9d2c-93d4da44fc57","30":"instance--6a1fca3c-fdb6-536a-bbea-61ac2349a700","300":"instance--043a5b44-2864-5565-abce-1909204e5485","330":"instance--e10eb918-2b0b-56f4-9c82-f345ce21276c","60":"instance--33a99d1b-dad8-51f6-be74-e1614db9151b","90":"instance--380c79e9-b1eb-547c-bf01-a011db1201c1"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--1","properties":[["name","Target KRBTGT after DC compromise"],["description","While the account is disabled and technically can\u2019t be enabled, it is often one of the first accounts an attacker goes after once a Domain Controller has been compromised."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0007","technique":"T1087.002"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--4f4d03a8-4502-5010-997b-9943e254395b","120":"instance--cefe62ac-5b6e-5ead-84fc-b4c632913a73","150":"instance--4d07a740-2467-5b95-ac8d-4a2ee8edd11e","180":"instance--1205f03c-a457-5a0b-87ef-3bbb7aac110f","210":"instance--96e7dc6a-9f86-5f69-8d45-a566303cd4c0","240":"instance--66237af6-bb19-5a51-9fa2-cbc4a96186f5","270":"instance--836dfd42-b475-50ca-9acf-4f11bd32b89f","30":"instance--efe92997-cc5c-538a-90bc-c09ffb1379f4","300":"instance--9c4a24ae-1426-5cb5-9d7c-792e6dd325b7","330":"instance--06c6a74a-ca7d-5703-88ea-a06a0933d21a","60":"instance--5e4f84e5-56b7-5b8f-9bc3-b4d59d371123","90":"instance--019deb6a-bab3-57db-9a53-11e3564bf7a4"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--2","properties":[["name","Obtain KRBTGT hash"],["description","Key to this is that you need the hash for the KRBTGT account which exists in every Active Directory domain. The KRBTGT account is the account used to generate and sign every Kerberos ticket in the domain."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0006","technique":"T1003.006"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0ce35aea-35a2-52ae-a67b-985306bdefe7","120":"instance--312639d5-e6d9-57b1-850d-28f0a1eac2f6","150":"instance--9551a25e-2558-512e-9894-dd64a8d662bf","180":"instance--403becce-e0ad-5dcd-bc14-7c00453907da","210":"instance--2305f501-2712-5ec6-9d4e-1371b011e937","240":"instance--cf1b8cf6-1cbd-5afb-b653-aa693889dab5","270":"instance--1d3dc59a-40a0-5670-aa3e-1304ff762003","30":"instance--77063d4f-503a-5e9b-b622-15aa2cc6a8e7","300":"instance--beaab67f-8a54-5982-8c5d-9d2ed2d42c9f","330":"instance--4d3274ff-ef14-5a53-99be-01575194a98e","60":"instance--4154a6bf-290b-5fce-a557-5dc0f3e700fb","90":"instance--2992bc0b-df57-54e5-a17b-03a964338c09"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--3","properties":[["name","Generate Golden Ticket"],["description","The \u201c method enables an attacker to create their own TGT using the KRBTGT account password hash ( ) with a long lifetime (10 years perhaps) and with any group membership they wish \u2013 remember, the TGT is encrypted/signed by the domain\u2019s KRBTGT account which is trusted by default by all computers in the domain."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1558.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--0f6e4da7-a5f4-54d7-866f-3bc6e8bcb019","120":"instance--015254b5-0906-577e-b3e3-3899f837d118","150":"instance--f7af5b8c-330a-58d5-b0da-a3d5f0bc6ad0","180":"instance--9f27ab21-2382-567d-b022-74ad5a29bd08","210":"instance--d799eb0a-7600-5b1a-a298-c47a78ceae4b","240":"instance--911c2c52-5974-5e08-b0b6-a9084d57c6ee","270":"instance--286444b4-97a1-58cd-9ca3-cffa04a15351","30":"instance--92192c38-5143-50e0-8c39-a96ea86e32e2","300":"instance--82bb3de0-bea5-5651-a1de-583283258c6d","330":"instance--4f0945c8-f644-50ce-8796-fea52a29dda1","60":"instance--16c43a2d-7356-521d-a507-5922e2c3337b","90":"instance--abce5c62-339a-5ed5-a0b8-dd66136cfe2f"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--4","properties":[["name","Request TGS with forged TGT"],["description","The brilliant part of creating a Golden Ticket (GT)\u00a0 using the domain KRBTGT hash is that the Golden Ticket contains whatever options the creator specifies and the KDC receiving the Golden Ticket generates a TGS assuming that all info in the Golden Ticket is valid."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0005","technique":"T1558.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--a469636c-0cb2-50b9-92f9-644c8aa98197","120":"instance--d57b3a21-e910-5879-8148-40165cea451a","150":"instance--58250ef4-5bb4-5bf3-b33e-89493bbb395d","180":"instance--3e769cf2-c1e5-5d2e-81d4-892f48ce4d86","210":"instance--f6499e41-749c-5d7f-9346-96c08d0d5dfd","240":"instance--d9dcdfc8-5f42-546a-803a-0efcd5d4cf91","270":"instance--c9afd0f6-97ce-57b2-9d60-3557b6214809","30":"instance--75f82155-f5ff-5619-8bf8-aae22937cab0","300":"instance--25e2d26e-1b35-56bd-b9aa-096c2d3b0e3c","330":"instance--e0483688-da10-5376-8cf2-050bcc3b70f0","60":"instance--1293d9cc-16b2-5c67-a453-bd144aab133a","90":"instance--2b43cd52-10db-5b15-8ad5-c4b59496528b"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--5","properties":[["name","Access resources with forged ticket"],["description","Since Kerberos tickets are only validated after 20 minutes (for Kerberos service ticket, TGS), an attacker has more than enough time to access data and/or resources. If not, the attacker can always generate a new \u201cGolden\u201d TGT."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0001","technique":"T1078"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--54fc1f38-f4e3-523e-b07c-73889b0d8df7","120":"instance--9cf45948-7040-5d7a-a1d5-3cb4db0c1af6","150":"instance--13bb13cc-e02b-51d2-8d7d-40e5613b6e5a","180":"instance--e33bc6ee-771e-54fe-a772-74dfdaad420d","210":"instance--286f51a3-8fc6-55ec-978e-8b05ebda3655","240":"instance--14659696-be77-5460-beb1-4b5eac126e43","270":"instance--f48ed1a6-2895-5cd2-9b1c-e30ac2bc8921","30":"instance--7b803e61-16ac-5720-92cd-8f2a456a52b7","300":"instance--76c24361-5143-5c43-8e4d-707c619e6038","330":"instance--f395cfc7-395a-5001-9552-a4fec6dbc53a","60":"instance--760885bb-9294-5a5b-93a2-a410e1ea4112","90":"instance--8e0d1a12-8611-598d-9a7d-40f2525e4781"},"id":"action","instance":"attack-action--6","properties":[["name","Persist despite password resets"],["description","The attacker may use the KRBTGT account to persist on the network even if every other account has its password changed."],["confidence",0.0],["ttp",{"tactic":"TA0003","technique":"T1558.001"}]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--35652c79-2c41-5d60-81ba-b5e47aa554bf","120":"instance--53906203-fffb-5af3-b112-44a9b4b49b8f","150":"instance--465fbc8a-7b4c-569f-be00-c0fbc137fcfc","180":"instance--a653c96b-3673-5dfa-968e-188fffe4cc04","210":"instance--6a344cf5-bd5c-52db-84f5-23c7701c7a5e","30":"instance--913561d1-b5f3-54d2-8272-159233dfde54","330":"instance--d59fe52d-c897-5f3a-919a-c2273cb8a8b3","60":"instance--f1fd6a3d-bb83-543d-a379-39d4632978f7","90":"instance--4cd6fce2-0d24-57f0-b161-12a867cd1100","branch:False":"instance--f7e897b3-3607-5ea5-8d15-5f83ba8a60da","branch:True":"instance--39b5ac19-b0dd-5674-a7d9-d75e659fe9ea"},"id":"condition","instance":"attack-condition--1","properties":[["description","While the account is disabled and technically can\u2019t be enabled, it is often one of the first accounts an attacker goes after once a Domain Controller has been compromised."]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--d820ed8c-cbdb-5429-b020-cea509c28489","120":"instance--52440b17-41c3-5b84-841d-db756bf19b1f","150":"instance--e4c2aea8-bf3e-5303-8134-234b623ba390","180":"instance--78cdfb51-4e1c-5df3-b9f9-d79593d60bee","210":"instance--b0ee06aa-f666-5e55-9240-74fccaa74166","240":"instance--58b5a41d-dde4-5875-826b-6f76ed798419","270":"instance--43314089-baff-54a3-be7d-3c25ac3e9d3d","30":"instance--6e981524-6d16-5070-96c6-391756917bcd","300":"instance--cc2c20ef-eb37-590f-b25c-357c4482516c","330":"instance--372c0f53-2e56-51da-af74-ee11152b84d9","60":"instance--33f8f019-9950-56b1-914e-4b12ccc1297c","90":"instance--6a79c49e-8ad5-5c77-bffa-b4dafc8cee91"},"id":"user_account","instance":"instance--61de4ecc-fa23-5e7e-ae06-4dea6f8fa7bb","properties":[["user_id","KRBTGT"],["account_login","KRBTGT"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"AD uses the KRBTGT account in the AD domain for Kerberos tickets.","source":"https://adsecurity.org/?p=483"}]]],["display_name","KRBTGT"],["diagram_instance","instance--61de4ecc-fa23-5e7e-ae06-4dea6f8fa7bb"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--cf74002f-0919-5e20-82d0-a66a53f84276","120":"instance--b57ac8ca-5ff0-53e0-a14c-7f563d376ec7","150":"instance--10d14fe8-2ff1-5a97-a833-9a639ad0e84d","180":"instance--716ebdbb-434d-56b1-a00b-c3a8a80a85d5","210":"instance--744383ac-7bd8-5cee-b645-ddbc13b5fca7","240":"instance--c66caa3a-edc1-53dd-9e60-aca3814b50c1","270":"instance--9e03c9da-417b-5b72-b81b-5b248aa7290e","30":"instance--e10a4564-60bc-5c0c-a7a8-40d2c5c6840f","300":"instance--601ecd24-d785-554d-a86d-2578b831ab52","330":"instance--e34c15f0-fed0-549c-a74e-178660bdc2fe","60":"instance--0c383bed-9abe-5fce-a549-a576368cc8f5","90":"instance--660e89cb-8d86-519a-82c1-636604ff3d72"},"id":"software","instance":"software--ad-domain-controller","properties":[["vendor","Microsoft"],["evidence",[["item-1",{"excerpt":"Every Domain Controller in an Active Directory domain runs a KDC (Kerberos Distribution Center) service which handles all Kerberos ticket requests.","source":"https://adsecurity.org/?p=483"}]]],["display_name","Domain Controller"],["name","Domain Controller"]]},{"anchors":{"0":"instance--742a0c4e-c73f-59f6-b2c0-f24d2d6b0324","120":"instance--68eb5ba0-0281-587b-a30a-fb179757f551","150":"instance--e3a57ae1-c422-5f1f-9d29-9e1caadb13a9","180":"instance--05f45f09-7a38-5df7-8c52-d990525d1150","210":"instance--22ce0442-00e1-51ae-a8ef-363c0b58f8c4","240":"instance--02f338a0-9adb-5bec-8dfe-a05cd4ad841d","270":"instance--ff10f3a9-35a4-55f9-88e7-c0117f0a0f55","30":"instance--2e0957da-4fd6-5870-b17a-d302922595a5","300":"instance--56fb9c59-3602-5047-a651-e644d79f59dc","330":"instance--67cdbab8-28d6-5a32-8629-b5ebe1bd6607","60":"instance--7ad20734-03c7-5177-87cf-7064a959ba80","90":"instance--3bdd3161-843b-5ab1-af1d-0d7417d49274"},"id":"user_account","instance":"instance--0f98e79d-d02b-5946-bd01-ed4